# SRG-APP-000156-AU-002380  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must use FIPS-validated SHA-1 or higher hash
# function to provide replay-resistant authentication mechanisms for network
# access to privileged accounts.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000156-AU-002380
group:           V-206465
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-001941
control_rev5:    IA-2

contribution:    Splunk can be placed in FIPS mode, which restricts it to FIPS-validated
                 algorithms, and Splunk Web can be configured to serve only over TLS with a
                 named server certificate and private key, so the authenticated session
                 over which privileged users log on is protected by a FIPS-validated hash.

governs:         splunk-launch.conf - Environment settings read before Splunk starts, including whether it
                 starts in FIPS mode.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
check:           web.conf [settings] enableSplunkWebSSL equals true
check:           web.conf [settings] serverCert non_empty
check:           web.conf [settings] privKeyPath non_empty
check:           web.conf [settings] serverCert not_equals $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/auth/splunkweb/cert.pem
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS equals 1 -> splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enableSplunkWebSSL https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] privKeyPath https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] serverCert https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Whether the named certificate was issued under DoD PKI, which is a
                 function of the issuing certificate authority and not readable from Splunk
                 configuration
external:        The FIPS-validated cryptographic module supplied with the platform, and
                 the kernel FIPS state of the host
external:        Replay resistance on the host's own network access paths, such as SSH,
                 carried by the operating system

citation:        SPLK-CL-000330 check and fix text (web.conf enableSplunkWebSSL = 1 with
                 privKeyPath and serverCert) and SPLK-CL-000390 fix text (SPLUNK_FIPS = 1
                 in splunk-launch.conf); splunk-launch.conf.spec:110-130 (SPLUNK_FIPS
                 vocabulary [0|1], one-time setting); web.conf.spec:70-73
                 (enableSplunkWebSSL, default false), web.conf.spec:75-91 (privKeyPath and
                 serverCert defaults point at the auto-generated pair)
finding:         Splunk is not in FIPS mode (splunk-launch.conf SPLUNK_FIPS is not 1), or
                 Splunk Web is not configured for TLS with a named server certificate and
                 private key, so the application does not provide a FIPS-validated
                 replay-resistant authentication channel for privileged network access.
